From 59673cb4617c3b1f659b048d9b36a88c408b4f58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:48:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS4: VLD1/VST1 a whole register at a time; longer idle spins
 on pinned cores; SVC and ioctl timing

- dynarmic A32: VLD1/VST1 (one element a structure, little-endian) as one 64-bit access a D
  register, an even D register and the next as one Q value (Pack2x64To1x128 / SetVector,
  GetVector / VectorGetElement64), instead of an access, shift and merge per element.
- PhysicalCore::Idle: 1 ms spin on emulated cores 0-2 when threads are pinned (EDEN_PS4_PIN_THREADS),
  50 us otherwise.
- PS4Perf::svc_cores: each SVC's count and whole time by core (Svc::Call); nvdrv Ioctl1's own time
  per ioctl in the service-call table.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VdsH7Cki1YqWbFL1ncEV7C
